<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Shields</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wear &lt;shield&gt;
</pre>
<p>A shield, worn on your arm, can turn aside blows and some spells. Each 
time you are hit, you may get your shield in the way:
</p>
<ul><li>against most weapons, and spells such as fireball, a good block <b>stops the blow entirely</b>: the shield takes the damage instead;</li>
<li>against the morning star and the flail, and spells such as firestorm, the shield only <b>softens</b> the blow;</li>
<li>and against the whip, and spells such as the poison gases and lightning, a shield is <b>no use</b> at all.</li></ul>
<p>Each spell's help says which of these it is.
</p><p>How often you block depends on:
</p>
<ul><li>the size of the shield: small, medium, large or tower, from about one block in seven for a small shield to one in three for a tower shield;</li>
<li>its craftsmanship and magic (see <a cmd='#'>Help Craftsmanship</a>);</li>
<li>your skill with shields, the shield skill, which most fighting guilds teach, against your attacker's own;</li>
<li>being able to see your attacker, and being awake.</li></ul>
<p><br />
See Also:
